# docs/ is ignored by default with an explicit whitelist -- only the files named
# below are tracked; everything else under docs/ stays local scratch. Git never
# descends into an ignored DIRECTORY, so re-including a file in a subdirectory
# requires un-ignoring each parent directory first (that is what the alternating
# `!/docs/<dir>/` + `/docs/<dir>/*` pairs are doing).
/docs/*
!/docs/architecture.md
!/docs/headless-updates.md
!/docs/linux.md
!/docs/linux-support-plan.md
!/docs/master-headless-re.md
!/docs/unity_cup.md
!/docs/scenarios/
/docs/scenarios/*
!/docs/scenarios/grand-live-endpoints.md
!/docs/superpowers/
/docs/superpowers/*
!/docs/superpowers/plans/
/docs/superpowers/plans/*
!/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-13-multi-account-frontend.md
!/docs/superpowers/specs/
/docs/superpowers/specs/*
!/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-13-multi-account-frontend-design.md
